{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1459545616,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNDUyODczODU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/393","origin":"github"},"title":"dataverse","message":"Might be cool to try.  There is an API (eg to fetch info for a dataset using persistent id https://dataverse.harvard.edu/api/datasets/:persistentId?persistentId=doi:10.7910/DVN/ARKOTI, https://github.com/IQSS/dataverse/issues/1837#issuecomment-197468164) and then we could use search mechanism (need API token) http://guides.dataverse.org/en/4.3/api/search.html to fetch listing of datasets (I guess eventually we could ask for an API cmd for that too ;)).\nIt is an interesting one since it is also distributed, hierarchical (we could use dataverse server as first level, two levels from doi) and would be a good check for scalability.  https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataverse/harvard lists 60k datasets from 1000 dataverses.  Some data there is even neuroimaging related (a few MRI/DTI/... studies).\nShould be an easy thing to setup IMHO... and would be somewhat an ideal case for scalability testing, especially whenever we start dealing with metadata","files":null}]}